{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 4.5% a year from $70.3 billion in FY2016 to $104.8 billion in FY2025 [F1][F10][F205], but the path was a step change, not a smooth climb."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Revenue jumped 19.8% in FY2020 and 13.3% in FY2021 [D183][D230], then fell 1.6%, 0.8% and 1.7% in FY2023 through FY2025 [D324][D370][D416]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2020 surge came from a 19.3% comparable sales increase and new stores, with the pandemic shifting category and channel mix [P51]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The recent decline reflects a 2.6% comparable sales decrease in FY2025, driven by a 2.2% drop in traffic and a 0.4% drop in average transaction [P14]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Merchandise sales are 98.0% of revenue in FY2025 [D465] and subtracted 2.0pp from growth that year [D467]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Food & beverage is the largest growing category at 23.0% of revenue [D506], adding 0.3pp in FY2025 [D508], while apparel fell 4.7% and subtracted 0.7pp [D564][D565]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The filings attribute the discretionary weakness to sales declines in Apparel & Accessories, Hardlines and Home Furnishings & Decor, partly offset by Frequency categories [P30]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income fell 8.1% in FY2025 against a 1.7% revenue decline [D417][D416], so there was no operating leverage; operating income compounded at only 0.6% over the window [F207]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted EPS compounded at 6.3% against net income's 3.4% [F210][F208], as diluted shares fell from 582.5 million to 455.6 million [X107][X116]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin was 4.9% in FY2025 [F34], below the 5.6% window median [D590] and far under the 8.4% FY2021 high [D589]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The FY2025 margin fell 0.3pp [D429], with cost of revenue taking 0.3pp and SG&A adding 0.1pp [D440][D441]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Gross margin fell to 27.9% from 28.2% on the net impact of several items the filing lists without quantifying [P12]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The SG&A rate held at 20.6% only because of a 0.6pp interchange settlement benefit; excluding it, the adjusted rate rose to 20.9% on sales deleverage [P11]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The effective tax rate rose to 22.3% from 22.2% on global minimum taxes and share-based compensation expense [P9][D403]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow was $6.56 billion and free cash flow $2.84 billion in FY2025 [F84][F104], a 2.7% FCF margin against the 4.5% window median [D401][D596]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow covered net income only 0.77x [D405], below the 1.01x window median [D599] and the 0.93x peer median [D615]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The operating cash flow decline reflects lower net earnings plus lower accounts payable leverage and inventory purchases [P7]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Capex rose 28.9% to $3.73 billion, or 3.6% of revenue [D423][F94][D400], and was 1.19x D&A [D406]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net debt was $4.30 billion, or 4.1% of revenue [D410][D411], better than the retail peer median of -3.5% net cash and at the 50th percentile of six peers [D613][D612]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Cash and investments reached $10.1 billion against $14.4 billion of debt [D408][D409], and the current ratio was 0.94x [F184]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Buybacks plus dividends of $2.46 billion were 86.8% of free cash flow [D412][D413], with buybacks cut to $408 million [X126]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Return on average equity was 24.0% [D415], below the 28.6% peer median and the 40th percentile of five peers [D617][D616]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Revenue has now fallen three years running, from $109.1 billion in FY2022 to $104.8 billion in FY2025 [F7][F8][F9][F10], a persistent top-line erosion [R1]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The current ratio sits at 0.94x [F184], below 1.0x and at the window median [D602], leaving little liquidity cushion [R2]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin has slipped two years in a row, 0.4pp in total [F32][F33][F34][R4], consistent with the deleverage the filing describes [P11]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "The FY2022 buyback figure was later restated to $2.65 billion from $2.83 billion [R5][X123]; the pack uses the first-reported value, so capital-return ratios for that year are approximate."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "If operating margin in the FY2026 10-K falls below the 4.9% FY2025 level [F34], the two-year slide becomes a structural margin problem rather than a cyclical one."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "If free cash flow margin stays below the 4.5% window median [D596], the 86.8% payout of FCF [D413] becomes harder to sustain."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Capex guidance of about $5 billion for FY2026 [P4] against FY2025's $3.73 billion [F94] would push capex near 4.8% of revenue if sales hold at $104.8 billion [F10], testing the cash conversion trend."}
  ]}
]}
